      heading: "A checklist before you hand in",
      body: "Statement questions carry many marks, so a routine helps. First, read the adjustments before you start writing and mark each trial balance item they affect. Second, write full headings with the business name, the statement name and the date or period. Third, prepare the statement of profit or loss in the standard order and show workings for any adjusted figure in brackets or in a separate working.\n\nFourth, prepare the statement of financial position using the three-column layout for non-current assets. Fifth, check that the profit for the year you carry into the capital section is the same figure you calculated. Sixth, check that total net assets equals closing capital. If they differ, find the difference and ask which single adjustment would explain it. A difference equal to the closing inventory, an accrual or the depreciation charge points straight to the missing entry.\n\nFinally, re-add every column. Most lost marks in this topic are arithmetic slips, not misunderstandings. Two minutes of re-adding can save several marks.",
