  examTips: [
    "Begin with the subscriptions account. It is usually worth several marks on its own and its answer feeds the income and expenditure account.",
    "Work through the receipts and payments account line by line and write next to each item where it goes: income, expenditure, asset, liability or activity trading account.",
    "Show the activity trading account separately and transfer the profit as one line. Label it profit on refreshments or profit on dance.",
    "Add the year's depreciation on equipment bought during the year if the question says depreciation is based on cost at the year end. Read the depreciation instruction twice.",
    "To find the opening accumulated fund, list only the assets and liabilities that existed at the start of the year. Do not include items bought during the year.",
    "Finish with the check: opening accumulated fund plus surplus equals net assets at the year end. If it does, say so; if not, look for an adjustment missed in one statement.",
  ],
